# Architecture

This is an Expo SDK 57 React Native project written in TypeScript.

Before making changes, follow the project's `AGENTS.md`.

## Feature-first organization

- Organize code using feature-first architecture.
- Feature-specific code belongs only inside its feature folder.
- Shared reusable code belongs in `src/shared`.

## Layering

- Screens should be thin and only compose components and hooks.
- Business logic belongs in hooks, reducers, services, or domain modules.
- Never duplicate business logic.

## Design principles

- Prefer composition over inheritance.
- Prefer small reusable components.
- Favor explicit, readable code over clever abstractions.
- Don't create abstractions until there are at least two real use cases.

## Refactors

- Preserve existing behavior during refactors.
- Never perform large architectural rewrites without explaining the plan first.
